<p>I found it all very readable, but there was one thing that stood out to me as soon as I read it: Every time this cancer spreads, it explicitly distorts and overtakes structures to the point of near unrecognizability, and yet the photo that it started from is still so intact and in shape that we can see who is in it and what they're doing? No one else has mentioned this, so if I just missed something, let me know. Maybe this is just one of those things for which you hope your readers will suspend disbelief, and if so, that's fair, but maybe it will be useful for you just to know that it stood out to me. :)</p>

							</div>

								
					
